WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.421
The travelers laid the soaked scrolls on some rocks.

2
00:00:07.422 --> 00:00:10.978
"The sun will dry them out," said Wukong.

3
00:00:10.979 --> 00:00:13.235
[g@The Tang Monk moaned.

4
00:00:13.236 --> 00:00:15.748
"What if they're ruined?"@g]

5
00:00:15.749 --> 00:00:19.329
He sat down and put his head in his hands.

6
00:00:19.330 --> 00:00:24.204
"I wish I'd remembered to ask Buddha the turtle's question!"

7
00:00:24.205 --> 00:00:26.670
[g@Bajie snorted.

8
00:00:26.671 --> 00:00:29.708
"Who cares if you forgot the turtle's question?@g]

9
00:00:29.709 --> 00:00:33.934
That turtle had no right to dump us in the water!"

10
00:00:33.935 --> 00:00:37.839
"Dumping us in the water was rude," Wujing agreed.

11
00:00:37.840 --> 00:00:40.382
Bajie sighed.

12
00:00:40.383 --> 00:00:45.256
"The journey back east is becoming just as difficult as the journey west."

13
00:00:45.257 --> 00:00:47.672
"Hello!" cried a voice.

14
00:00:47.673 --> 00:00:52.652
The travelers turned and saw a man hurrying toward them.

15
00:00:52.653 --> 00:00:54.967
[g@"Chen," said the Tang Monk.

16
00:00:54.968 --> 00:00:57.573
He grasped the man's hands.@g]

17
00:00:57.574 --> 00:01:00.084
"It's good to see you again."

18
00:01:00.085 --> 00:01:03.617
"It's good to see all of you." Chen smiled.

19
00:01:03.618 --> 00:01:06.563
"Did you reach the Western Paradise?"

20
00:01:06.564 --> 00:01:08.818
"Yes," said the Tang Monk.

21
00:01:08.819 --> 00:01:10.770
[g@"It was magnificent!

22
00:01:10.771 --> 00:01:13.660
The land is filled with beauty."@g]

23
00:01:13.661 --> 00:01:19.188
Chen noticed the scrolls lying on the rocks, and his eyes went wide.

24
00:01:19.189 --> 00:01:23.830
"Are those the True Scriptures?" he whispered.

25
00:01:23.831 --> 00:01:25.873
[g@"Yes," said the monk.

26
00:01:25.874 --> 00:01:30.808
"But as you can see, they got wet."@g]

27
00:01:30.809 --> 00:01:36.614
"A giant turtle dumped us in the river," added Bajie with a sigh.

28
00:01:36.615 --> 00:01:39.262
"Please come with me," said Chen.

29
00:01:39.263 --> 00:01:42.246
"You can dry the True Scriptures by my fire.

30
00:01:42.247 --> 00:01:47.052
Everyone in the village will be excited to see the travelers who met Buddha."

31
00:01:47.053 --> 00:01:51.043
Wujing started gathering the wet scriptures.

32
00:01:51.044 --> 00:01:54.024
"I'll help you," said Bajie.

33
00:01:54.025 --> 00:01:57.332
[g@The pig grabbed a scroll and pulled.

34
00:01:57.333 --> 00:02:00.089
But it was stuck to a rock.@g]

35
00:02:00.090 --> 00:02:06.866
[i@Rip!@i] The corner of the scroll tore off.

36
00:02:06.867 --> 00:02:11.199
The Tang Monk gasped. "Oh no!"

37
00:02:11.200 --> 00:02:15.606
Bajie stared in horror at the torn scroll.

38
00:02:15.607 --> 00:02:20.022
Wukong smiled. "Don't worry, Master."

39
00:02:20.023 --> 00:02:24.155
The monkey gently picked the rest of the scroll off the rock.

40
00:02:24.156 --> 00:02:26.448
"The scroll is fine."

41
00:02:26.449 --> 00:02:29.438
"But it's ripped!" cried the monk.

42
00:02:29.439 --> 00:02:33.113
Bajie hung his head.

43
00:02:33.114 --> 00:02:35.545
[g@"Tell me something, Master," said Wukong.

44
00:02:35.546 --> 00:02:38.103
"Are you perfect?"@g]

45
00:02:38.104 --> 00:02:41.532
[g@The monk gave Wukong a confused look.

46
00:02:41.533 --> 00:02:43.522
"Of course not."@g]

47
00:02:43.523 --> 00:02:47.091
"Am I perfect?" asked the monkey.

48
00:02:47.092 --> 00:02:51.236
The Tang Monk shook his head.

49
00:02:51.237 --> 00:02:55.155
[g@"How about Bajie?" Wukong smirked.

50
00:02:55.156 --> 00:02:58.743
"We all know he's not perfect."@g]

51
00:02:58.744 --> 00:03:01.437
The pig snorted.

52
00:03:01.438 --> 00:03:05.351
"Nothing on Earth or in Heaven is perfect," said Wukong.

53
00:03:05.352 --> 00:03:08.961
"So why should the True Scriptures be any different?

54
00:03:08.962 --> 00:03:13.083
They'll teach the people of the East how to be good and avoid suffering.

55
00:03:13.084 --> 00:03:21.446
They will also teach the people that nothing needs to be perfect."

56
00:03:21.447 --> 00:03:29.557
The travelers finished gathering the scrolls and followed Chen back to the village.

57
00:03:29.558 --> 00:03:33.653
People came out of their homes to see the travelers.

58
00:03:33.654 --> 00:03:36.475
"Welcome back!" called a woman.

59
00:03:36.476 --> 00:03:40.954
"It's wonderful to see you all again!" shouted an old man.

60
00:03:40.955 --> 00:03:48.387
Soon a crowd was following the Tang Monk and his companions to Chen's house.

61
00:03:48.388 --> 00:03:52.692
That evening the villagers held a big feast.

62
00:03:52.693 --> 00:03:57.599
Later that night Wukong and the Tang Monk sat, talking.

63
00:03:57.600 --> 00:04:00.209
"We must leave soon," said the monk.

64
00:04:00.210 --> 00:04:03.628
"The villagers will want to see the True Scriptures.

65
00:04:03.629 --> 00:04:07.031
They'll become jealous that we have them."

66
00:04:07.032 --> 00:04:09.685
"I agree," said Wukong.

67
00:04:09.686 --> 00:04:15.196
He remembered the priest who'd tried to kill the Tang Monk and steal the robe.

68
00:04:15.197 --> 00:04:19.853
"Let's sneak away now, while the villagers are asleep," said Wukong.

69
00:04:19.854 --> 00:04:24.181
The monk and the monkey woke up Bajie and Wujing.

70
00:04:24.182 --> 00:04:28.496
The group sneaked out of Chen's house and headed east.

71
00:04:28.497 --> 00:04:33.921
It was dark, but the light from the full moon lit up the road.

72
00:04:33.922 --> 00:04:38.088
Suddenly the guard from the Thunderclap Monastery appeared.

73
00:04:38.089 --> 00:04:41.684
[g@"Congratulations!" said the guard.

74
00:04:41.685 --> 00:04:45.554
"You have faced one hundred challenges."@g]

75
00:04:45.555 --> 00:04:49.338
[g@"Whew." The monk sighed with relief.

76
00:04:49.339 --> 00:04:52.459
"I will become a buddha at last."@g]

77
00:04:52.460 --> 00:04:55.494
[g@The guard recited a spell.

78
00:04:55.495 --> 00:05:05.379
Once again the travelers flew toward the East.@g]

